title: Light/dark theme system and academia dark mode fix
summary: Added site-wide light/dark mode toggle with localStorage persistence and flash-prevention script. Fixed academia (university) theme which was applying light-mode palette (cream/parchment text colors) on dark backgrounds because the dark variant required a data-theme="auto" attribute that was never set. Reworked academia.css to default to dark, with light mode gated behind data-theme="light". Fixed header background using hardcoded rgba instead of theme tokens.
symbols_touched:
  - '#SiteHeader'
  - '#ObsidianTheme'
  - '#AcademiaTheme'
  - '#SiteApp'
symbols_created:
  - '#ThemeToggle'
files_created:
  - packages/site/src/components/ThemeToggle.tsx
files_modified:
  - packages/site/src/tokens/obsidian.css
  - packages/site/src/tokens/academia.css
  - packages/site/src/components/SiteHeader.tsx
  - packages/site/src/components/SiteHeader.module.css
  - packages/site/src/app/layout.tsx
decisions:
  - id: D-dark-default
    decision: Dark mode is the default, not system preference
    rationale: The site identity is built around the obsidian dark theme. Light mode is opt-in via toggle, not auto-detected from OS preference.
  - id: D-blocking-script
    decision: Use blocking inline script to set data-theme before paint
    rationale: Prevents flash of wrong theme on page load. The script reads localStorage synchronously before React hydrates.
  - id: D-color-mix
    decision: Use CSS color-mix for header transparency instead of hardcoded rgba
    rationale: Header background needs to adapt to theme. color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-1) 85%, transparent) gives the translucent glass effect in both modes.
learnings:
  - Academia theme dark mode was broken since creation — the CSS required data-theme='auto' which nothing ever set
  - Hardcoded rgba values in CSS are theme-breaking landmines — always use token variables
  - color-mix() is well-supported and perfect for translucent theme-aware backgrounds
verification:
